# Files Semgrep should skip entirely.
#
# scripts/fetch-catalogs.ts is a Node build-time helper invoked only via
# `npm run fetch-catalogs` (and as the `prebuild` step, which the GitHub
# Pages deploy now runs). It is never bundled into the SPA or executed in
# users' browsers. The execSync call inside `run()` is composed from the
# framework list in `public/config.json` — a repo-controlled file read at
# build time, never user input — so the `detect-child-process` rule is a
# false positive. Inline `// nosemgrep` directives are not honored by
# `semgrep ci` v1.163.0 in this CI configuration, so the suppression
# lives here instead.
scripts/fetch-catalogs.ts
